Package: bridgeoverlap
Type: Package
Title: Overlap Certificates and Failure Diagnostics for Bridge Sampling
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Giorgio", "Micaletto", email = "gmicaletto@uchicago.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Diagnostics for the optimal bridge sampling estimator of
    Meng and Wong (1996). The estimator is computed as the root of the score of
    an intercept-only logistic regression that separates posterior from proposal
    draws. From the fitted responsibilities the package computes, at no extra
    cost, the delta-method Monte Carlo standard error (MCSE) with a within-chain
    long-run variance, the effective overlap certificate, a finite-sample
    confidence interval for independent draws based on Bennett's inequality, a
    calibration test for sampler failure and delete-a-group jackknife
    diagnostics for Markov chain output. Works directly on objects returned by
    'bridgesampling::bridge_sampler()' and provides helpers for 'cmdstanr' fits,
    including two-fold cross-fitting.
